{"name":"Van de Cane","hex":"#faf7eb","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"van","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Valman."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A covered motor vehicle used to carry goods or (normally less than ten) persons, usually roughly cuboid in shape, Depending on the type of van, it can be bigger or smaller than a pickup truck and SUV, and longer and higher than a car but relatively smaller than a truck/lorry or a bus.","An enclosed railway vehicle for transport of goods, such as a boxcar/box van."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/van"},{"term":"cane","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant with simple stems, like bamboo or sugar cane, or the stem thereof:\n The slender, flexible main stem of a plant such as bamboo, including many species in the grass family Gramineae.","The slender, flexible main stem of a plant such as bamboo, including many species in the grass family Gramineae."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To strike or beat with a cane or similar implement.","To make or furnish with cane or rattan."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cane"}],"entries":[{"title":"Van (Dutch)","blocks":[{"text":"Van is a very common prefix in Dutch surnames, where it is known as a tussenvoegsel. In those cases it nearly always refers to a certain, often quite distant, ancestor's place of origin or residence; for example, Ludwig van Beethoven \"from Beethoven\" and Rembrandt van Rijn \"from the Rhine\". Van is also a preposition in the Dutch and Afrikaans languages, meaning \"of\" or \"from\" depending on the context."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Van_(Dutch)","wikidata":"Q1258618"},{"title":"Van","blocks":[{"text":"A van is a type of road vehicle used for transporting goods or people. There is some variation in the scope of the word across the different English-speaking countries. The smallest vans, microvans, are used for transporting either goods or people in tiny quantities. Mini MPVs, compact MPVs, and MPVs are all small vans usually used for transporting people in small quantities. Larger vans with passenger seats are used for institutional purposes, such as transporting students. Larger vans with only front seats are often used for business purposes, to carry goods and equipment. Specially equipped vans are used by television stations as mobile studios. Postal services and courier companies use large step vans to deliver packages."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/2018_Ford_Transit_Custom_300_Base_2.0_facelift.jpg/330px-2018_Ford_Transit_Custom_300_Base_2.0_facelift.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Van","wikidata":"Q193468"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Roger_Fenton%27s_waggon.jpg/500px-Roger_Fenton%27s_waggon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Roger_Fenton%27s_waggon.jpg/1280px-Roger_Fenton%27s_waggon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Roger_Fenton%27s_waggon.jpg/500px-Roger_Fenton%27s_waggon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Roger Fenton's photographic van, Crimea, 1855","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoger_Fenton's_waggon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Toyota_Hiace_H200_505.JPG/500px-Toyota_Hiace_H200_505.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Toyota_Hiace_H200_505.JPG/500px-Toyota_Hiace_H200_505.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Toyota HiAce cab over van","link":"https://en.wiki